From: Vincent Donnefort <vdonnefort@google.com>
Date: Fri Mar 7 14:58:46 2025 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Fix iommu CMA pool fast-forward

When allocating pages from one of the CMA pool, we might store an
out-of-bound value as the next pool to allocate from. Fix it.

Bug: 383901011
Bug: 277989609
Bug: 278749606
Fixes: 3f35c377b90d ("ANDROID: KVM: arm64: iommu: Allow donations from a CMA pool")
Change-Id: I3ff021640d8a1140bfbbe65153bbb3667529409f
Signed-off-by: Vincent Donnefort <vdonnefort@google.com>

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 6e4a686138484e3e9909820551900cab22d507c5
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class A, apply as-is; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
index dbc1938..13a15b1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
@@ -79,14 +79,14 @@ void *kvm_iommu_donate_pages(u8 order, bool request)
 
 	i = last_block_pool;
 	do {
-		p = hyp_alloc_pages(&iommu_block_pools[i++], order);
+		p = hyp_alloc_pages(&iommu_block_pools[i], order);
 		if (p) {
 			last_block_pool = i;
 			hyp_spin_unlock(&__block_pools_lock);
 			return p;
 		}
 
-		if (i >= MAX_BLOCK_POOLS)
+		if (++i >= MAX_BLOCK_POOLS)
 			i = 0;
 	} while (i != last_block_pool);
 
